# W44-65 memo predicted 3 codec_wiki cells closing (e7 d=4, 5, 6) with
# its 22-cell A/B sweep showing −1.36 % / −3.25 % / −1.59 % bytes vs the
# pinned-off variant. In the full ledger refresh (vs cjxl baseline), the
# closure breakdown is:
#
# | cell              | jxl B (W44-65) | cjxl B  | delta % | status |
# | ---               | ---            | ---     | ---     | ---    |
# | codec_wiki e7 d=4 | 64936          | 62710   | +3.55 % | OPEN   |
# | codec_wiki e7 d=5 | 57314          | 57232   | +0.14 % | FIXED  |
# | codec_wiki e7 d=6 | 53078          | 51875   | +2.32 % | FIXED  |
#
# d=4 sits +3.55 % bytes — just over the 3.0 % byte threshold and bfly
# +7.19 %. W44-65 brought it down from W44-64's +4.98 %, but didn't
# fully cross the parity line. Acceptable per the 17-19 OPEN buffer
# given in the W44-66 spec.

